  "contract_id": "V09B-MODERN-GAME-RELEASE-ROSTER-SOURCE-PROBE-V1",
  "status": "SOURCE_CLASS_SEMANTIC_VIABILITY_PROBE_ONLY_NO_COVERAGE_OR_QUALIFICATION_AUTHORITY",
  "purpose": "Test whether week-specific first-party NFL club Game Release / Weekly Release packets provide a dated, independently enumerated current roster with separately labeled practice-squad and reserve populations. This probe tests source-class semantics only. It does not prove locator coverage, does not classify game-day eligibility, and does not authorize labels or model fitting.",
  "hypothesis": "A week-specific official club release can provide an independently enumerated active-or-current roster population rather than defining positives by absence from an inactive list. If the roster snapshot predates kickoff and excluded populations are explicitly separated, a later locator/chronology audit may test whether these packets can serve as the base state for game-day eligibility reconstruction.",
